      "explain": "Two graphs G1 and G2 are <strong>isomorphic</strong> if there is a one-to-one, onto mapping (a bijection) between their vertex sets that <strong>preserves adjacency</strong> — that is, u and v are joined in G1 <em>if and only if</em> their images f(u) and f(v) are joined in G2. In plain words: same structure, different names and different drawing.",
