      "title": "Shortest Path in a Weighted Graph — Dijkstra's Algorithm",
      "teacher": "This is the exact algorithm running inside Google Maps when it tells you the fastest way to college. It is also beautifully simple: always walk to the nearest place you have not visited yet, and keep updating your best-known distances. Let us do one fully on the board.",
      "explain": "<strong>Dijkstra's algorithm</strong> finds the shortest path from one starting vertex to every other vertex in a weighted graph with <strong>non-negative</strong> weights. It keeps a tentative distance for each vertex, repeatedly picks the unvisited vertex with the smallest distance, marks it final, and uses it to improve (<strong>relax</strong>) its neighbours' distances.",
