      "realLife": "You are at Bhopal railway station and want the cheapest auto route to UIT-RGPV with three possible stops on the way. Dijkstra says: go to the nearest reachable stop first, note down the cheapest cost to reach each of the others through it, and keep repeating. You never have to try every possible route.",
      "worked": "<strong>Find the shortest path from A to every vertex.</strong><br>V = {A, B, C, D, E}<br>Weighted edges: A–B = 4, A–C = 2, B–C = 1, B–D = 5, C–D = 8, C–E = 10, D–E = 2<br><br><strong>Initialise:</strong> A = 0; B = C = D = E = ∞. Nothing visited.<br><br><strong>Step 1 — visit A (0), the smallest.</strong><br>Relax A–B: 0 + 4 = 4 &lt; ∞ → <strong>B = 4</strong> (via A)<br>Relax A–C: 0 + 2 = 2 &lt; ∞ → <strong>C = 2</strong> (via A)<br>Table now: A=0✔, B=4, C=2, D=∞, E=∞<br><br><strong>Step 2 — smallest unvisited is C (2). Visit C.</strong><br>Relax C–B: 2 + 1 = 3 &lt; 4 → <strong>B improves to 3</strong> (via C)<br>Relax C–D: 2 + 8 = 10 &lt; ∞ → <strong>D = 10</strong> (via C)<br>Relax C–E: 2 + 10 = 12 &lt; ∞ → <strong>E = 12</strong> (via C)<br>Table now: A=0✔, B=3, C=2✔, D=10, E=12<br><br><strong>Step 3 — smallest unvisited is B (3). Visit B.</strong><br>Relax B–D: 3 + 5 = 8 &lt; 10 → <strong>D improves to 8</strong> (via B)<br>Table now: A=0✔, B=3✔, C=2✔, D=8, E=12<br><br><strong>Step 4 — smallest unvisited is D (8). Visit D.</strong><br>Relax D–E: 8 + 2 = 10 &lt; 12 → <strong>E improves to 10</strong> (via D)<br>Table now: A=0✔, B=3✔, C=2✔, D=8✔, E=10<br><br><strong>Step 5 — visit E (10). All vertices visited. Stop.</strong><br><br><strong>Final shortest distances from A:</strong><br>A = 0 · B = <strong>3</strong> · C = <strong>2</strong> · D = <strong>8</strong> · E = <strong>10</strong><br><br><strong>Trace the route to E backwards:</strong> E came from D, D came from B, B came from C, C came from A.<br>→ Shortest path <strong>A → C → B → D → E</strong><br><em>Check the arithmetic:</em> 2 + 1 + 5 + 2 = <strong>10</strong> ✅ matches the table.<br><em>Compare the obvious route</em> A → C → E = 2 + 10 = 12, which is longer — so the detour really was cheaper.",
