      "examAnswer": "Dijkstra's algorithm determines the shortest path from a given source vertex to all other vertices in a weighted graph in which every edge weight is non-negative. The algorithm assigns a tentative distance of zero to the source and infinity to every other vertex. At each stage it selects the unvisited vertex having the smallest tentative distance, marks it as visited so that its distance becomes final, and then relaxes each edge leaving it, that is, for every unvisited neighbour it replaces the neighbour's tentative distance by the smaller of the existing value and the distance of the current vertex plus the weight of the connecting edge. The process is repeated until all vertices have been visited, and the shortest route is recovered by tracing the recorded predecessors backwards from the destination.",
